{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Review on Save",
  "description": "Analyzes modified source code files for potential improvements including code smells, design patterns, and best practices. Generates suggestions for improving readability, maintainability, and performance while maintaining existing functionality.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "*.py"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified code for potential improvements. Focus on:\n1. Code smells (long methods, duplicated code, overly complex logic)\n2. Design pattern opportunities (where patterns could simplify or improve the code)\n3. Best practices (naming conventions, error handling, type hints, documentation)\n4. Readability improvements (clearer variable names, better structure, simpler expressions)\n5. Maintainability concerns (tight coupling, missing abstractions, hard-coded values)\n6. Performance optimizations (inefficient loops, unnecessary allocations, better data structures)\n\nProvide concise, actionable suggestions that maintain existing functionality. Prioritize the most impactful improvements."
  }
}